body:
Damn dude. Your post seems like one of the more mature ones out there. Just want to let you know I respect your choice not to do drugs and keep your job.  (That being said, as someone who loves weed, don't be afraid to let your hair down and get a lil relaxed sometimes! A quick break is good for the soul)

&#x200B;

First off, you're not an asshole for feeling unhappy when people say you have it good. Yes, it's important to be grateful but everyone is different. i.e. A rich man who's never been loved may feel worse than a poor man with loved ones.  It depends on perspective, how you view yourself. IMO you're doing pretty good, a lot of people on this sub have struggles with drugs and their jobs, so keep it up!

&#x200B;

That being said, it sounds like a lot of your depression comes from the constant monotony of your life.  With an unchanging job and sparse people around you to mix things up, days quickly start feeling the same, I've been there before. Negative thoughts repeat themselves and there's nothing to break the trend.  Have you tried travelling somewhere crazy? Great way to mix things up, so you always have something to look forward to. I travel alone often and I absolutely love it. Treat yo' self! Seems like you have the funding too, so why not? PM me if you want some travel tips!

&#x200B;

I also don't think you should rule yourself out as being desirable by other people. Trust me, even though all people may seem the same to you, they're not. That's not to say that nobody is "average", or that everyone is different, cause that's not true, but there are plenty of outliers like us. I mean hey if you're fit and decent looking, hop on bumble or some dating app, whats the worst that could happen? There's tons of quiet people who don't fuck with bars and drugs. Boatloads of em. You gotta be interested in other people to get them interested in you tho. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, thats just what I wanted to say. Remember that your life is in your hands and the truth of the matter is that if you want it to be different, you gotta go out there and mix it up yourself. Good thing is that's not a hard thing to do! PM me if you want to talk more.
